\pard\sb240\sa120\keepn\b\fs34 EIR request to the Environment Agency \u8212- three matters\b0\fs22\par
\par
\pard {\b Send to:} {\f1 enquiries@environment-agency.gov.uk} Copy to {\f1 Enquiries_WestMids@environment-agency.gov.uk} (public-register enquiries for the Trent permits).\par
\par
\pard {\b Subject:} EIR request \u8212- permit T/61/09188/O, flow monitoring at Milnhay (Heanor) STW, and river sampling on the Erewash\par
\par
\pard Three matters in one letter, numbered so they cannot be answered as one. Opening with the Environmental Information Regulations wording starts a {\b 20 working day} clock; without it this is just correspondence and can sit.\par
\par
\pard Send the same questions to Severn Trent as well \u8212- {\f1 customer.relations@severntrent.co.uk}, or 0800 783 4444. {\b If the two answers differ, that is more interesting than either on its own}, and Part B is exactly the kind of question where they might.\par
\par
