\par
\pard I can find no record of this asset in the Event Duration Monitoring Storm Overflow Annual Return for any year from 2021 to 2025. I have searched those returns by permit reference, by site name and by grid reference. The nearest entry to the recorded discharge point is a different outfall on a different permit (Cromford Road CSO No 3, T/61/12266/O), 280 metres away.\par
\par
\pard I do not believe this is a category that falls outside the return: "Storm discharge at pumping station" appears in the 2025 return 3,318 times nationally.\par
\par
\pard {\b A1.} Is this permit still in use? If it relates to an asset that no longer exists, why does it remain on the register as active with no revocation date?\par
\par
\pard {\b A2.} If it is in use, is an Event Duration Monitor fitted? If so, under what unique identifier is it reported, so that I can find it?\par
\par
\pard {\b A3.} If no monitor is fitted, why not, and when will one be installed?\par
\par
\pard {\b A4.} How many hours has this outfall discharged into the River Erewash in each of the last five calendar years, and how many separate discharges were there?\par
\par
\pard {\b A5.} Please provide a copy of the current permit and any variations to it.\par
\par
